            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "There are $28-2=26$ students doing at least one activity. Of the 9 doing both Football and Gardening, $9-5=4$ do not do Instrumental Music.\n\nLet $x$ be the number doing only Gardening. Then $2x$ do only Football. The 16 students in $I$, the two exclusive regions, and the 4 doing Football and Gardening without Instrumental Music are disjoint and account for all 26 participants.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}26&=16+2x+x+4\\\\26&=20+3x\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus 4 do only Football. Let $n$ be the number doing Football and Instrumental Music but not Gardening.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=18-4-4-5\\\\n&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, 5 students do Football and Instrumental Music but not Gardening.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
